# Discuss trade-offs first

Before fixing or adding a feature, say the options in plain language and what each costs. Do not silently pick a path when the user has not stated a priority.

Cover, when they apply:

- Speed / lag (extra API vs local work vs main-thread work)
- Accuracy / reliability
- Battery or always-on resources (mic engine, timers, network)
- Complexity (rules you must maintain vs one model prompt)

If the user already stated a priority (e.g. “no extra lag”), follow it and still name the trade-off in one line.

Example: spoken punctuation — local regex (no wait, you list every word) vs LLM pass (understands slash/plus automatically, only if Correction is already on).
